    "description": "<section class=\"product-intro\">\n<h3>The Tee</h3>\n<p>You put on a Peculiar People shirt because it reminds you why we're all here. Because that building is where you were sealed to your spouse, where you got an answer to a prayer you'd been carrying for years, where you first felt something you couldn't explain away. A stepping stone. A day you'll never forget.</p>\n<p>You put it on because you want to share that with someone. Because gospel conversations are hard to start. Harder than they were on your mission, when the whole day was built around them.</p>\n<p>It's the new white shirt and tie. The new dress. The new name tag you don't need a calling to wear. A shirt you may even feel prompted to wear some days.</p>\n<p>That's why I started this company. It doesn't take much for someone who has been prepared to tap you on the shoulder and ask a question that changes the direction of their life. No argument, no pitch, no lesson plan. Just an opening.</p>\n<p>And you keep it on because it's premium heavyweight ringspun cotton, garment-dyed to that soft, worn-in vintage look you'd wear even if it said nothing at all.</p>\n<p>- Evan</p>\n<p><strong>Weight:</strong> 6.1 oz/yd&sup2;<br><strong>Fabric:</strong> preshrunk 100% ring-spun cotton</p>\n<p><strong>Fit:</strong> Relaxed, true to size.<br><br><strong>Tighter fit:</strong> size down 1 size<br><strong>Regular fit: </strong>your actual size<br><strong>Relaxed fit:</strong> size up 1 size<br><strong>Loose fit: </strong>size up 2 sizes<br><strong>Oversize fit:</strong> size up 3 sizes<br><br></p>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"size-guide\">\n<h3>Size Guide</h3>\n<video autoplay=\"autoplay\" loop=\"loop\" muted=\"\" playsinline=\"\" preload=\"none\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:800px;height:auto;aspect-ratio:1/1;margin:0 auto\">\n<source src=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/videos/c/o/v/af9f7c981a7942008b118c687e992e5e.webm\" type=\"video/webm\">\n<source src=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/videos/c/o/v/f2d223d1c3e34b0b93ae98a8efb07d29.mp4\" type=\"video/mp4\"></source></video>\n<br>\n<h4>Measurements (inches)</h4>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"col\">Size</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Width</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Length</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"row\">S</th>\n<td>18.25</td>\n<td>26.62</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"row\">M</th>\n<td>20.25</td>\n<td>28</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"row\">L</th>\n<td>22</td>\n<td>29.37</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"row\">XL</th>\n<td>24</td>\n<td>30.75</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"row\">2XL</th>\n<td>26</td>\n<td>31.62</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"row\">3XL</th>\n<td>27.75</td>\n<td>32.5</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"row\">4XL</th>\n<td>29.75</td>\n<td>33.5</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Width is measured underarm to underarm. Length is measured from the collar to the bottom of the shirt.</p>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"temple-facts\">\n<h3 class=\"temple-facts__name\">Draper Utah Temple</h3>\n<p class=\"temple-spec__row\"><strong>Location</strong><br>Draper, Utah, on a hillside at the south end of the Salt Lake Valley, below Corner Canyon.</p>\n<p class=\"temple-spec__row\"><strong>Temple Number</strong><br>The 129th dedicated temple.</p>\n<p class=\"temple-spec__row\"><strong>Announced</strong><br><time datetime=\"2004-10-02\">October 2, 2004</time>, by President Gordon B. Hinckley, in the Saturday morning session of general conference.</p>\n<p class=\"temple-spec__row\"><strong>Groundbreaking</strong><br><time datetime=\"2006-08-05\">August 5, 2006</time>. President Gordon B. Hinckley presided and dedicated the site.</p>\n<p class=\"temple-spec__row\"><strong>Dedicated</strong><br><time datetime=\"2009-03-20\">March 20</time> to <time datetime=\"2009-03-22\">22, 2009</time>, by President Thomas S. Monson.</p>\n<p class=\"temple-spec__row\"><strong>Architecture</strong><br>FFKR Architects. Temple white granite from China with bronze doors. 58,300 square feet, rising 168 feet 8 inches to the top of the gold leafed angel Moroni statue.</p>\n<p class=\"temple-spec__row\"><strong>Ordinance Rooms</strong><br>Four instruction rooms in a two stage progressive arrangement, five sealing rooms, one baptistry.</p>\n<h4>Construction Story</h4>\n<ul class=\"temple-facts__list\">\n<li>Four and a half years passed between the announcement and the dedication, with construction running from August 2006 into early 2009.</li>\n<li>The public open house ran <time datetime=\"2009-01-15\">January 15</time> through <time datetime=\"2009-03-14\">March 14, 2009</time>, excluding Sundays, and drew 684,721 visitors.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Symbolism &amp; Design</h4>\n<ul class=\"temple-facts__list\">\n<li>The sego lily, Utah's state flower, recurs throughout the building in art glass by Utah artist Tom Holdman and in the decorative painting.</li>\n<li>The art glass also carries a Log Cabin quilt pattern. The building holds 221 exterior windows, 50 interior windows and 432 door panels, made up of 35,420 hand cut pieces of glass.</li>\n<li>Makore wood, imported from the west coast of central Africa, is used in the doors, trim, paneling and cabinets. Limestone from France appears elsewhere in the interior.</li>\n<li>Hand painted panoramas by Utah and Colorado artists show mountain scenes, Draper's Corner Canyon and views across the Salt Lake Valley.</li>\n<li>The baptistry sits on the downhill western side, with floor to ceiling windows that fill it with daylight.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Trivia</h4>\n<ul class=\"temple-facts__list\">\n<li>One of the sealing rooms seats up to 80 guests.</li>\n<li>Nearly 685,000 people toured the temple across the two month open house.</li>\n</ul>\n<p class=\"temple-facts__asof\"><em>Temple facts verified as of <time datetime=\"2026-08-20\">August 20, 2026</time>.</em></p>\n</section>"
